://miqllcwiki.com/blog/how-wikipedia-editors-review-articles#webpage\",\"name\":\"How Wikipedia Editors Review Articles\",\"description\":\"Learn how Wikipedia editors evaluate new and existing articles, including sourcing, notability, neutrality, and policy compliance.\",\"url\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/how-wikipedia-editors-review-articles\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/#website\"},\"about\":{\"@id\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/#organization\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Insights\",\"item\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"How Wikipedia Editors Review Articles\",\"item\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/how-wikipedia-editors-review-articles\"}]}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BlogPosting\",\"@id\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/how-wikipedia-editors-review-articles#article\",\"headline\":\"How Wikipedia Editors Review Articles\",\"description\":\"Learn how Wikipedia editors evaluate new and existing articles, including sourcing, notability, neutrality, and policy compliance.\",\"url\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/how-wikipedia-editors-review-articles\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/how-wikipedia-editors-review-articles#webpage\"},\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"@id\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/#organization\",\"name\":\"MIQ LLC\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"@id\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/#organization\",\"name\":\"MIQ LLC\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/favicon.svg\"}},\"datePublished\":\"2026-11-10\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-11-10\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https://miqllcwiki.com/#website\"},\"keywords\":[\"how Wikipedia editors review articles\",\"Wikipedia article review\",\"Wikipedia editorial process\",\"Wikipedia notability review\",\"Wikipedia reliable sources\"],\"hasPart\":{\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Is there an official Wikipedia approval team?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Wikipedia content is generally reviewed by community editors through various processes. There is no single approval path that guarantees publication for every article.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What makes editors keep an article?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Strong independent sourcing, clear notability, neutral writing, verifiable claims, and compliance with Wikipedia policies improve an article’s quality. However, no factor guarantees that an article will be kept.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can an article be changed after it is published?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. Wikipedia articles can be edited by others over time. Changes should be based on reliable sources and follow content policies.\"}}]}}</script><section class=\"hero-grid text-white\"><div class=\"grid-lines\"><div class=\"container-tight py-20 md:py-24\"><nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"mb-4 text-sm text-white/65\"><ol class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2\"><li><a class=\"hover:text-white\" href=\"/\">Home</a></li><li aria-hidden=\"true\">/</li><li><a class=\"hover:text-white\" href=\"/blog\">Insights</a></li><li aria-hidden=\"true\">/</li><li class=\"text-white/85\">How Wikipedia Editors Review Articles</li></ol></nav><p class=\"mb-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-electric\"><span class=\"text-sky-300\">Wikipedia<!-- --> Guide</span></p><h1 class=\"font-display max-w-4xl text-4xl font-semibold md:text-5xl\">How Wikipedia Editors Review Articles</h1><p class=\"mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg text-white/78\">Wikipedia articles are reviewed through community editorial processes, not a single centralized approval team. Editors look for reliable sources, notability, neutral writing, policy compliance, and clear evidence that the article belongs in an encyclopedia.</p><p class=\"mt-4 text-sm text-white/60\">Published <!-- -->2026-11-10<!-- --> · Updated <!-- -->2026-11-10</p></div></div></section><section class=\"section-pad \"><div class=\"container-tight grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[.28fr_.72fr]\"><aside class=\"lg:sticky lg:top-28 lg:self-start\"><div class=\"rounded-3xl border border-border bg-surface p-5\"><p class=\"font-display text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-electric\">On this page</p><ul class=\"mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-muted\"><li><a href=\"#community-process\" class=\"hover:text-navy\">Review is community-driven</a></li><li><a href=\"#what-editors-check\" class=\"hover:text-navy\">What editors commonly check</a></li><li><a href=\"#possible-outcomes\" class=\"hover:text-navy\">Possible outcomes after review</a></li><li><a href=\"#prepare-for-review\" class=\"hover:text-navy\">How to prepare before review</a></li><li><a href=\"#faqs\" class=\"hover:text-navy\">Frequently asked questions</a></li><li><a href=\"#references\" class=\"hover:text-navy\">References</a></li></ul></div></aside><article class=\"max-w-3xl\"><section id=\"community-process\" class=\"mb-10 scroll-mt-28\"><h2 class=\"font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-navy md:text-3xl\">Review is community-driven</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-base leading-8 text-muted\"><p>Wikipedia is edited by a volunteer community, and review can happen in different ways. Articles may be created, improved, tagged, discussed, revised, or nominated for deletion depending on their quality and sourcing. Drafts may also receive feedback through submission or review processes.</p><p>Because many editors can participate, there is no single path that guarantees the same result for every topic. The quality of sources and the neutrality of writing are usually central to how an article is evaluated.</p></div></section><section id=\"what-editors-check\" class=\"mb-10 scroll-mt-28\"><h2 class=\"font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-navy md:text-3xl\">What editors commonly check</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-base leading-8 text-muted\"><p>Editors often assess whether the topic is notable, whether claims are verifiable, and whether sources are reliable and independent. They may also check tone for promotional language, evaluate whether the article has a conflict-of-interest appearance, and look for copyright or close paraphrasing issues.</p><p>For business and biography topics, sourcing and neutrality receive particular attention. An article that is technically well-formatted but based on weak or non-independent sources may still be challenged.</p></div></section><section id=\"possible-outcomes\" class=\"mb-10 scroll-mt-28\"><h2 class=\"font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-navy md:text-3xl\">Possible outcomes after review</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-base leading-8 text-muted\"><p>An article may be expanded, improved, merged, redirected, kept with cleanup tags, or deleted. Feedback can range from minor citation requests to concerns about notability or promotional content. Outcomes depend on evidence, policy application, and editorial discussion.</p><p>If concerns are raised, improving sources and neutrality is often more productive than disputing the process with unsourced arguments. In some cases, the correct outcome may be to wait until stronger independent coverage exists.</p></div></section><section id=\"prepare-for-review\" class=\"mb-10 scroll-mt-28\"><h2 class=\"font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-navy md:text-3xl\">How to prepare before review</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-base leading-8 text-muted\"><p>Preparation should include a source inventory, claim-by-claim verification, neutral wording, and careful handling of any conflict of interest. Drafts should be concise and limited to what reliable independent sources support.</p><p>A policy-aware pre-submission review can identify issues early, but it cannot control how independent editors respond. The goal is to submit accurate, well-sourced material that can withstand scrutiny.</p></div></section><section id=\"faqs\" class=\"mb-10 scroll-mt-28\"><h2 class=\"font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-navy md:text-3xl\">Frequently asked questions</h2><div class=\"mt-5\"><div class=\"divide-y divide-border rounded-2xl border border-border bg-white\"><details class=\"group\" open=\"\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 text-left [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden\"><span class=\"font-medium text-navy\">Is there an official Wikipedia approval team?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down shrink-0 text-muted transition group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm leading-6 text-muted\">Wikipedia content is generally reviewed by community editors through various processes. There is no single approval path that guarantees publication for every article.</div></details><details class=\"group\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 text-left [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden\"><span class=\"font-medium text-navy\">What makes editors keep an article?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down shrink-0 text-muted transition group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm leading-6 text-muted\">Strong independent sourcing, clear notability, neutral writing, verifiable claims, and compliance with Wikipedia policies improve an article’s quality. However, no factor guarantees that an article will be kept.</div></details><details class=\"group\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 text-left [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden\"><span class=\"font-medium text-navy\">Can an article be changed after it is published?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-down shrink-0 text-muted transition group-open:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"></path></svg></summary><div class=\"px-5 pb-5 text-sm leading-6 text-muted\">Yes. Wikipedia articles can be edited by others over time. Changes should be based on reliable sources and follow content policies.</div></details></div></div></section><section id=\"references\" class=\"mb-10 scroll-mt-28 rounded-3xl border border-border bg-surface p-6\"><h2 class=\"font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-navy\">References</h2><p class=\"mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-muted\">External references are provided for general guidance. Wikipedia policies and community practices can change, so review the current source pages before making decisions.</p><ul class=\"mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm\"><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Editing_policy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-electric hover:underline\">Wikipedia: Editing policy</a></li><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Policies_and_guidelines\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-electric hover:underline\">Wikipedia: Policies and guidelines</a></li><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Notability\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-electric hover:underline\">Wikipedia: Notability</a></li><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Reliable_sources\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-electric hover:underline\">Wikipedia: Reliable sources</a></li><li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Articles_for_creation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-electric hover:underline\">Wikipedia: Articles for creation</a></li></ul></section><div class=\"rounded-3xl bg-navy p-7 text-white\"><p class=\"text-lg font-semibold\">Preparing a draft for editorial review?</p><a class=\"mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full bg-white px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-navy\" href=\"/services/wikipedia-services\">Get Article Preparation Guidance<!-- --> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-arrow-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 12h14\"></path><path d=\"m12 5 7 7-7 7\"></path></svg></a></div></article></div></section><!--$--><!--/$--><!--/&--><!--/&--><!--/&--></main><footer class=\"border-t border-white/10 bg-navy text-white\"><div class=\"container-tight grid gap-10 py-14 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4\"><div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 64 64\" fill=\"none\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"h-9 w-9\"><rect width=\"64\" height=\"64\" rx=\"16\" fill=\"#0B1B33\"></rect><path d=\"M18 44V20h6.2l7.8 12.2L39.8 20H46v24h-5.7V29.4l-8.3 12.8-8.3-12.8V44H18Z\" fill=\"white\"></path><path d=\"M46 44c0-4.2 3.2-7 7.6-7 .1 0 .3 0 .4 0v5c-.2 0-.4-.1-.7-.1-1.6 0-2.7.8-2.7 2.5V44H46Z\" fill=\"#C8A24A\"></path><circle cx=\"48.5\" cy=\"17.5\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#3B82F6\"></circl