rs keep an article?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Strong independent sourcing, clear notability, neutral writing, verifiable claims, and compliance with Wikipedia policies improve an article’s quality. However, no factor guarantees that an article will be kept.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can an article be changed after it is published?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. Wikipedia articles can be edited by others over time. Changes should be based on reliable sources and follow content policies.\"}}]}}24:[[[\"$\",\"script\",\"0\",{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"WebPage\\\",\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/how-wikipedia-editors-review-articles#webpage\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"How Wikipedia Editors Review Articles\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Learn how Wikipedia editors evaluate new and existing articles, including sourcing, notability, neutrality, and policy compliance.\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/how-wikipedia-editors-review-articles\\\",\\\"isPartOf\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https://miqllcwiki.com/#website\\\"},\\\"about\\\":{\\\"@id\\\":\\\"https://miqllcwiki.com/#organization\\\"},\\\"inLanguage\\\":\\\"en-US\\\"}\"}}],[\"$\",\"script\",\"1\",{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"BreadcrumbList\\\",\\\"itemListElement\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":1,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Home\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://miqllcwiki.com/\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":2,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Insights\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":3,\\\"name\\\":\\\"How Wikipedia Editors Review Articles\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://miqllcwiki.com/blog/how-wikipedia-editors-review-articles\\\"}]}\"}}],[\"$\",